    <section id="tab1" class="pd-tab-pane active" role="tabpanel">
      <div class="pd-section"><h3>Overview</h3>
        <p>Hull &amp; Machinery insurance covers physical loss to a vessel (hull, machinery and equipment) at sea or in port, together with collision liability.</p>
        <p>It applies to all vessel types — ocean-going and coastal vessels, fishing boats, passenger and cargo ships, tugs and work boats — and can be extended to Builder's Risk (under construction) and Submarine Cable.</p></div>
      <div class="pd-section"><h3>Applicable clauses</h3>
        <ul class="pd-feature-list">
          <li><span class="pd-num">01</span><div class="pd-ftext"><strong>ITC-Hulls</strong><p>Institute Time Clauses — Hulls (international standard).</p></div></li>
          <li><span class="pd-num">02</span><div class="pd-ftext"><strong>IVC-Hulls</strong><p>Institute Voyage Clauses — Hulls.</p></div></li>
          <li><span class="pd-num">03</span><div class="pd-ftext"><strong>Builder's Risk</strong><p>Cover for vessels under construction.</p></div></li>
          <li><span class="pd-num">04</span><div class="pd-ftext"><strong>Submarine Cable</strong><p>Laying and operation of submarine cables.</p></div></li>
        </ul></div>
      <div class="pd-section"><h3>Who needs it</h3>
        <ul class="pd-feature-list">
          <li><span class="pd-num">01</span><div class="pd-ftext"><strong>Ocean / coastal shipping lines</strong><p>Cargo ships, tankers, bulkers, container vessels.</p></div></li>
          <li><span class="pd-num">02</span><div class="pd-ftext"><strong>Fishing / marine industry</strong><p>Trawlers, tuna seiners, aquaculture work boats.</p></div></li>
          <li><span class="pd-num">03</span><div class="pd-ftext"><strong>Marine civil works / offshore</strong><p>Tugs, work boats, barges.</p></div></li>
          <li><span class="pd-num">04</span><div class="pd-ftext"><strong>Shipyards / owners (Builder's Risk)</strong><p>Risk during construction.</p></div></li>
        </ul></div>
    </section>
    <section id="tab2" class="pd-tab-pane" role="tabpanel">
      <div class="pd-section"><h3>Main losses covered</h3>
        <ul class="pd-bul">
          <li>Stranding, sinking, collision, capsizing</li>
          <li>Fire, explosion, lightning</li>
          <li>Piracy / robbery (with War endorsement)</li>
          <li>Machinery and navigation-equipment breakdown (Inchmaree Clause)</li>
          <li>Collision liability to third-party vessels / structures (3/4 Collision Liability)</li>
          <li>General average contribution and salvage</li>
          <li>Loss-prevention costs (Sue &amp; Labour)</li>
        </ul></div>
      <div class="pd-section"><h3>Main endorsements</h3>
        <ul class="pd-bul">
          <li>P&amp;I (separate) — crew injury, oil pollution and cargo liability via a P&amp;I Club</li>
          <li>War &amp; Strike — war, strike, riot</li>
          <li>Freight, Demurrage &amp; Defence — freight recovery and dispute defense</li>
          <li>Builder's Risk — risk during construction</li>
          <li>Submarine Cable — laying / operating submarine cables</li>
          <li>Port Risk — while berthed in port; TLO (Total Loss Only)</li>
        </ul></div>
      <div class="pd-exclude"><h4>Main exclusions</h4>
        <ul>
          <li>Wilful misconduct / gross negligence (inherent vice)</li>
          <li>Ordinary wear, tear, corrosion and ageing</li>
          <li>Unseaworthiness (where known to the insured)</li>
          <li>Insolvency of the owner</li>
          <li>Nuclear, biological or chemical weapons</li>
          <li>Seizure or detention by government / public authority</li>
          <li>Piracy / terrorism (without a War / Piracy endorsement)</li>
        </ul></div>
    </section>
    <section id="tab3" class="pd-tab-pane" role="tabpanel">
      <div class="pd-section"><h3>Conditions &amp; process</h3>
        <table class="pd-info-table">
          <tr><th>Period</th><td>1 year or by voyage</td></tr>
          <tr><th>Insurer</th><td>Hyundai Marine &amp; Fire (with Lloyd's reinsurance)</td></tr>
          <tr><th>Sum insured</th><td>Sound value of the vessel</td></tr>
          <tr><th>Channel</th><td>Individual consultation with our team (+82-10-5755-6465)</td></tr>
          <tr><th>Turnaround</th><td>Coastal / small: 1–2 weeks · ocean / large / submarine cable: 3–6 weeks</td></tr>
        </table></div>
      <div class="pd-section"><h3>What we need to quote</h3>
        <ul class="pd-bul">
          <li>Vessel registry and survey certificates</li>
          <li>IMO number and class certificate (KR / LR / DNV / ABS)</li>
          <li>Vessel valuation report</li>
          <li>Master and crew qualifications / experience; trading route</li>
          <li>Claims history for the last 5 years; proposal / questionnaire</li>
          <li>Evidence of P&amp;I cover</li>
        </ul></div>
      <div class="pd-section"><h3>Other notes</h3>
        <ul class="pd-bul">
          <li>Crew, oil-pollution and cargo liability require separate P&amp;I Club cover.</li>
          <li>Cover lapses if the class is suspended.</li>
          <li>A War / Piracy endorsement is essential for transits via the Red Sea, Hormuz or Somali waters.</li>
        </ul></div>
      <div class="pd-section"><h3>Cooling-off / duty of disclosure</h3>
        <ul class="pd-bul">
          <li>Cooling-off (cancellation) within 15 days of receiving the certificate (excluding professional financial consumers).</li>
          <li>Breach of the duty to explain material matters or a missing signature may allow cancellation within 3 months.</li>
          <li>Breach of the duty of disclosure may lead to cancellation or reduced indemnity.</li>
        </ul></div>
      <div class="pd-disclosure">
        <span class="deposit-protect">Depositor-protected product</span>
        <h3>Things to note</h3>
        <ul class="pd-bul">
          <li>This is non-life insurance promotional material; cover, exclusions and limits follow the <strong>policy wording and certificate</strong>.</li>
          <li><strong>Final premiums and terms are confirmed after the insurer's underwriting review.</strong></li>
          <li>We work with 6 AM Best A++–A rated insurers (AIG · Chubb · DB · Hyundai · KB · Meritz) and place each line with the insurer best suited to your risk — not merely the lowest price.</li>
          <li>Our brokerage fee is paid by the insurer and is not added to your premium (Article 98, Insurance Business Act).</li>
          <li>Full Korean statutory disclosures (depositor protection, fraud reporting, dispute resolution) are on the <a href="/products/marine-hull.html">Korean page</a>.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </section>

